{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"Run a program on the instance's own machine and wait for it, bounded by a real wall-clock timeout (the process is killed when it expires). argv form, no shell - pass [\"sh\", \"-c\", \"...\"] for shell syntax. Runs in the instance root. Returns FLAT {ok, exit_code, timed_out, stdout, stderr}: ok is true only on exit status 0; a spawn failure or timeout reports ok false with the reason in stderr (exit_code -1 when there is none). The local counterpart of ssh_run.","import":"use std::io::Read;\nuse std::process::{Command, Stdio};\nuse std::sync::mpsc;\nuse std::time::{Duration, Instant};\nuse ndata::dataobject::DataObject;","params":[{"desc":"The program and its arguments, one string per element, e.g. [\"ls\", \"-la\", \"runtime\"]. No shell: nothing is interpolated or globbed. For shell syntax (pipes, redirects, &&), pass [\"sh\", \"-c\", \"<command line>\"].","name":"argv","type":"JSONArray"},{"desc":"Wall-clock limit in seconds for the whole run; the process is killed when it expires. Pass 0 for the default of 60.","name":"timeout_secs","type":"Integer"}],"returntype":"FLAT","type":"rust"},"id":"nsuqxx1a0ed71e06bk1","readers":[],"time":1790690318090,"username":"system","writers":[]}